    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0037" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation 3/248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-07T19:00:00-05:00">January 7, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. For the Under Secretary. My telegram No. 18 of January 5, 11 p.m.<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d25-f1"/> In response to my inquiry Minister of Foreign
                    Relations this morning had no further information except his belief if [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">is</hi>] that resistance to a resolution calling on all
                    American Republics to break relations with the Axis would take as juridical
                    basis, “false though it be,” the thesis that the aggression had been committed
                    against islands outside this hemisphere.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
